Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Frobenius: joining and splitting group labels", \
"Subsubsection"]], "Title",ExpressionUUID->"2a60d4f9-b28e-4991-a955-\
b2ccaea448d4"],

Cell["\<\
The Frobenius condition says that three ways of joining and splitting labels \
give the same answer. We will see each term of that answer for the six \
permutations of three objects. The main calculation uses lists of group \
labels, not index contractions. Evaluate the cells in order in a fresh \
kernel. All definitions and saved outputs are here; no companion file is \
needed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4c583e09-0c58-429d-b020-48e3cf895a48"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Source: smsa.pdf v7.7, \[Section]17.2, Frobenius algebras, \
(17.35)\[Dash](17.38) and (17.42). This is a pedagogical adaptation of \
Symmetri2025/frobenius_condition.nb; the original is preserved. The matching \
v7.7 TeX and equation labels were unavailable. We work over the complex \
numbers, write ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["e", "g"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4e7227eb-edaa-4f54-b023-2a90f5d46211"],
 " for the notes' delta-function basis, and initially use coproduct scale c = \
1. Section 6 restores the exact normalization in (17.38). These are \
rescalings of the notes' example, not proposed corrections."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d3daea10-532a-4a9c-9dcb-90cbd7758f3d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. A basis vector carries a group label", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cc5716b1-a94d-4d72-b946-3d4f3e71c45f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"A", "\[LongEqual]", 
   RowBox[{"\[DoubleStruckCapitalC]", "(", 
    SubscriptBox["S", "3"], ")"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ac9f3941-00ac-4002-85a9-9008b275ac35"],
 ". There is one basis vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["e", "g"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d16e3176-0ff2-4169-98ba-8274b92d917d"],
 " for each permutation g. A general element is a complex linear combination \
of these six basis vectors. Multiplication joins two labels: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["e", "g"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
     SubscriptBox["e", "h"]}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
   SubscriptBox["e", 
    RowBox[{"g", " ", "h"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e4e38d9f-8f4c-4911-8062-0784b2440384"],
 ". The unit is the basis vector labelled by the identity permutation."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c8e8a710-f6c6-41dd-b73f-53b3157f85be"],

Cell["\<\
Represent a permutation by the images of 1, 2 and 3. Thus {2,1,3} swaps 1 and \
2. Our product applies the right permutation first: p[[q]] lists p(q(1)), \
p(q(2)), p(q(3)). Ordering[p] is the inverse permutation. The short names \
below are only for displaying answers.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5e62cbc1-80ee-4710-87ec-1d8de92cf980"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Clear", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "elements", ",", "identity", ",", "product", ",", "inverse", ",", "names", 
    ",", "name", ",", "split"}], "]"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"elements", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Permutations", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", "2", ",", "3"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"identity", "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "2", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], ";", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"product", "[", 
    RowBox[{"p_", ",", "q_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"p", "\[LeftDoubleBracket]", "q", "\[RightDoubleBracket]"}]}], ";", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"inverse", "[", "p_", "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"Ordering", "[", "p", "]"}]}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"names", "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<1\>\"", ",", "\"\<(23)\>\"", ",", "\"\<(12)\>\"", 
     ",", "\"\<(123)\>\"", ",", "\"\<(132)\>\"", ",", "\"\<(13)\>\""}], 
    "}"}]}], ";", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"name", "[", "p_", "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"names", "\[LeftDoubleBracket]", 
    RowBox[{"First", "[", 
     RowBox[{"FirstPosition", "[", 
      RowBox[{"elements", ",", "p"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
    "\[RightDoubleBracket]"}]}], ";", 
  TagBox[
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"elements", ",", "names"}], "}"}]},
    "Transpose"],
   Function[BoxForm`e$, 
    TableForm[
    BoxForm`e$, 
     TableHeadings -> {None, {"Images of 1,2,3", "Cycle name"}}]]]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[192]:=",ExpressionUUID->"007385b3-ba2f-405e-af9e-6158df87fa7e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", "2", ",", "3"}], "}"}], "\<\"1\"\>"},
     {
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", "3", ",", "2"}], "}"}], "\<\"(23)\"\>"},
     {
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", "1", ",", "3"}], "}"}], "\<\"(12)\"\>"},
     {
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", "3", ",", "1"}], "}"}], "\<\"(123)\"\>"},
     {
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"3", ",", "1", ",", "2"}], "}"}], "\<\"(132)\"\>"},
     {
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"3", ",", "2", ",", "1"}], "}"}], "\<\"(13)\"\>"}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
         Offset[0.7]}, 
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
        Offset[0.2], {
         Offset[0.4]}, 
        Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.000003044758218*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[192]=",ExpressionUUID->"f69c925e-19a6-4d22-b1de-c08b7989f2a3"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Choose two swaps that do not commute. Predict the two products by following \
each of the three objects, before evaluating this cell.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6af04a5d-9347-49b9-abb3-7d49e73d7404"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"g", "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "1", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"h", "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "3", ",", "2"}], "}"}]}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"name", "[", "g", "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"name", "[", "h", "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"name", "[", 
     RowBox[{"product", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", "h"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"name", "[", 
     RowBox[{"product", "[", 
      RowBox[{"h", ",", "g"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[193]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7590d387-33a4-4ebb-ae58-c37c3751d9e4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"(12)\"\>", ",", "\<\"(23)\"\>", ",", "\<\"(123)\"\>", 
    ",", "\<\"(132)\"\>"}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0000030447880363`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[193]=",ExpressionUUID->"c0ef1488-d47c-4f1b-9b9c-072995b9547c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The products are (123) and (132). Keeping their order is essential: our \
example is noncommutative. The Frobenius condition will hold anyway.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6093ee88-457f-4e8d-b673-5e1397e0f942"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. Splitting means listing every factorization", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"55177d67-8fba-4d86-85fd-abd4ccf7e9a1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At scale c = 1, define ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", "[", 
    SubscriptBox["e", "g"], "]"}], "=", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    RowBox[{"a", " ", "b", "=", "g"}]], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["e", "a"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    SubscriptBox["e", "b"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6a858cad-0acf-4192-abd8-4d8b711c2c84"],
 ". This notation means one term for each ordered pair (a,b) with ab = g, \
each with coefficient one. It is a sum of basis tensors, not a random choice \
of a factorization."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6c0c7fc3-2aec-414a-8aa0-043cd0734814"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We can list those pairs without solving equations: for every group element \
k take (gk, k inverse). Their product is g. Conversely, any factorization ab \
= g appears once, by choosing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"k", "\[LongEqual]", 
   TemplateBox[{"b", 
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}]},
    "Superscript"]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "fadca568-81ab-4288-807a-e4de8f322b91"],
 ". Hence there are exactly six terms."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3d722960-0932-4f47-b5de-92a44a131264"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"split", "[", "p_", "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"product", "[", 
        RowBox[{"p", ",", "k"}], "]"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"inverse", "[", "k", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", "elements"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
  TagBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"name", "/@", "#1"}], "&"}], ")"}], "/@", 
    RowBox[{"split", "[", "g", "]"}]}],
   Function[BoxForm`e$, 
    TableForm[
    BoxForm`e$, 
     TableHeadings -> {None, {"Left label a", "Right label b"}}]]]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[194]:=",ExpressionUUID->"35841163-3c2a-4044-9060-78c939bc4a95"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
     {"\<\"(12)\"\>", "\<\"1\"\>"},
     {"\<\"(123)\"\>", "\<\"(23)\"\>"},
     {"\<\"1\"\>", "\<\"(12)\"\>"},
     {"\<\"(23)\"\>", "\<\"(132)\"\>"},
     {"\<\"(13)\"\>", "\<\"(123)\"\>"},
     {"\<\"(132)\"\>", "\<\"(13)\"\>"}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
         Offset[0.7]}, 
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
        Offset[0.2], {
         Offset[0.4]}, 
        Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.000003044794057*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[194]=",ExpressionUUID->"fdac9588-f348-4fdc-9ae0-169ecb5c8ccf"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Association", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<Exactly six distinct terms\>\"", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
      RowBox[{"DeleteDuplicates", "[", 
       RowBox[{"split", "[", "g", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "\[Equal]", "6"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Every displayed pair multiplies to g\>\"", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"split", "[", "g", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"product", "@@", "#1"}], "\[Equal]", "g"}], "&"}]}], 
     "]"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[195]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b851a84a-52e6-469d-b168-82dead73739e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\<\"Exactly six distinct terms\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"Every displayed pair multiplies to g\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
     "True"}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}], TraditionalForm]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.000003044795918*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[195]=",ExpressionUUID->"f8229c13-ba76-452e-a489-e65f0ec5d755"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the identity label the six terms are the inverse pairs: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", "[", 
    SubscriptBox["e", "1"], "]"}], "=", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    RowBox[{"k", "\[Element]", 
     SubscriptBox["S", "3"]}]], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["e", "k"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    SubscriptBox["e", 
     SuperscriptBox["k", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}]]]}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "86d848f2-732f-4ca0-8fc7-cbc45149ec38"],
 ". This will also explain the unit and counit in Section 6."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d3b6c7c2-0159-4339-9c9f-f37016678643"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Three routes, with every term visible", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"da78cc78-021d-4d82-99ad-b2339906cfa6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two Frobenius equalities (17.35)\[Dash](17.36) can be written together \
as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"id", "\[CircleTimes]", "\[Mu]"}], ")"}], "\[SmallCircle]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", "\[CircleTimes]", "id"}], ")"}]}], "\[LongEqual]", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", "\[SmallCircle]", "\[Mu]"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[CircleTimes]", "id"}], ")"}], "\[SmallCircle]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"id", "\[CircleTimes]", "\[CapitalDelta]"}], ")"}]}]}]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"d034ec9e-230b-4bc6-8743-1b07cc0d66c0"],
 ". Each route has two inputs and two outputs. Read composition from right to \
left."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e9ea6680-1fe6-4802-9a40-217172ba859d"],

Cell["\<\
The three diagrams show the same routes. Read every wire upward: the two \
labels enter at the bottom and the two output labels leave at the top. The \
blue nodes mark the operation performed at that height.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"598df975-4806-4671-a9dd-adea987530c3"],

